5. Error Code Standard

Every known application failure must have a predefined error code.

Do NOT generate arbitrary error codes in individual classes.

Create a centralized error catalog.

Recommended format:

<DOMAIN>-<NUMBER>

Examples:

FILE-001
FILE-002
PREFUND-001
PREFUND-002
SETTLE-001
SETTLE-002
DB-001
DB-002
MQ-001
MQ-002
KAFKA-001
KAFKA-002
STORAGE-001
AUTH-001
AUTH-002
API-001
CONFIG-001
VALIDATION-001
RECOVERY-001
SYSTEM-001

Error codes must be:

* unique
* stable
* documented
* searchable
* machine-readable
* reusable.

Never reuse an error code for a materially different failure.

