18. Retryable vs Non-Retryable

Every known exception should be classified.

Retryable:
DB connection timeout
MQ unavailable
Kafka temporary failure
HTTP 503
Storage unavailable
Non-Retryable:
Invalid file format
Invalid business rule
Authorization failure
Malformed request
Amount mismatch
Duplicate business transaction

Do not retry business validation failures indefinitely.

⸻

19. Retry Logging

For retryable failures include:

retryable
retryCount
maxRetries
nextRetryAt
retryStrategy

Example:

{
  "errorCode": "MQ-001",
  "retryable": true,
  "retryCount": 2,
  "maxRetries": 5,
  "retryStrategy": "EXPONENTIAL_BACKOFF"
}

Do not log every retry at ERROR if it is an expected transient condition.

Recommended:

First failure → WARN
Repeated failure → WARN
Retry exhausted → ERROR
Business impact/critical outage → CRITICAL

