50. Final Principle

The logging implementation must not merely answer:

“What exception occurred?”

It must answer:

“What failed, where, between which components, why, what business state is affected, whether it can recover automatically, what the operator should investigate, and what action should be taken?”

The target operational model is:

ERROR CODE
    +
SOURCE → TARGET
    +
OPERATION
    +
CORRELATION
    +
BUSINESS CONTEXT
    +
ROOT CAUSE
    +
IMPACT
    +
FOCUS AREA
    +
REMEDIATION HINT
    +
RECOVERY STATE

This information must be available consistently across APIs, background workers, files, databases, MQ/Kafka, storage, Kubernetes/OpenShift, and multi-data-center processing.
